{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775511071,"nonce":"tpz3Y/NRHrQNX8rIW+EDLjlmLA4=","title":"Add file signal instructions to OpenHands prompt","message":"Add file signal instructions to OpenHands prompt\n\n## Context\nSignal protocol Phase 4: OpenHands cannot use MCP tools (framework bug strips arguments). File signals are confirmed working (tested 2026-04-06 on host and Docker). Add instructions to the OpenHands agent prompt telling it to write signal files instead of relying solely on native FinishAction mapping.\n\nDepends on: b8fef04 (file signal detection in SessionRunner)\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_prompts.py::test_openhands_prompt_includes_signal_instructions\n  Assert: when agent_kind is \"openhands\", the rendered prompt contains instructions about /session/signal/done\n- tests/test_prompts.py::test_non_openhands_prompt_no_signal_instructions\n  Assert: when agent_kind is \"claude-code\", the prompt does NOT contain /session/signal/ instructions\n\n## Files\n- core/prompts.py (modify — add file signal instructions for openhands agent kind)\n- templates/WORKFLOW.md (modify — add conditional signal instructions block)\n\n## Implementation\n1. In the prompt template (templates/WORKFLOW.md or core/prompts.py), add a conditional block:\n   ```\n   {% if agent_kind == \"openhands\" %}\n   ## Signal Protocol\n   When you complete the task, write a file at /session/signal/done containing a one-line summary.\n   If you have a question, write /session/signal/question.json with {\"question\": \"your question\"}.\n   For progress checkpoints, write /session/signal/checkpoint with a description.\n   These signal files are REQUIRED in addition to using FinishAction.\n   {% endif %}\n   ```\n2. Ensure the agent_kind variable is available in the Jinja2 template context (check core/prompts.py render function).\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee existing conditional blocks in templates/WORKFLOW.md.\nSee core/prompts.py for template rendering.\nSee docs/signal-protocol-design.md Phase 4 for confirmed test results.\n\n## Notes\n- FinishAction still works as before (mapped to @@DONE@@ by the adapter). File signals are additive.\n- File signals give SessionRunner a direct detection path that doesn't depend on stdout parsing.\n\nREQ: REQ-004","files":null}]}